  "id": "resistance-to-extinction",
  "term": "resistance to extinction",
  "definition": "Resistance to extinction is the tendency for a learned response to persist even when the cue is repeatedly presented without the outcome that originally gave it meaning. In this context, it refers to conditioned disgust being relatively hard to weaken through cue-only exposure.",
